@ 11.5 - Proto-Northeast Caucasian to Proto-Lezgic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from User:Petusek (2010), “User:Petusek/Drafts/Northeast Caucasian”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. NB: These changes here probably aren’t “proper” sound changes, whatever that’s supposed to mean, but there doesn’t seem to be any particular sound change or set of sound changes that defines this family, so I’ve elected to go with something that seems to nearly work and note the exceptions.
	{ q, ɢ } > { {x,q}, ɣ }